      "side": 1,
      "message": "Fixed in PS3 by replacing buildMsgpackReader\u003cSyncMsg\u003e with buildSyncMsgReader. It first runs the existing incremental MessagePack visitor API without constructing msgpack objects. Copy/reserve is bounded per wire object (8MiB), with bounded feed chunks, depth32 and 262144 declared child/object slots; hostile map32/array32 counts are rejected from their headers. The visitor separately checks metadata entries\u003c\u003d16384, keys\u003c\u003d1024 bytes, values\u003c\u003d65536 bytes, writer length64 and the existing 4MiB accounted budget BEFORE object-tree construction or map/string conversion. Only a complete preflighted message is unpacked with explicit parser limits. Metadata rules do not constrain unrelated preference strings, and multiple valid coalesced objects may exceed8MiB in aggregate. Invalid input/application error permanently closes the reader; callback exceptions propagate. Added regressions for header-only oversized declarations, oversize keys/values/writers, aggregate metadata/node budgets, deep/incomplete input, both legacy layouts, multiple coalesced large objects and callback failure. All24 reader/serialization cases pass in each layout.",
